.\" man/man3/Docv::Markdown.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Markdown" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Markdown \- Markdown documents: CommonMark with the GitHub extensions (tables, task lists, strikethrough, autolinks and alerts), parsed by markd into the same \fB\%Document\fR model as manual pages.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBmodule Docv::Markdown\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Markdown documents: CommonMark with the GitHub extensions (tables, task
lists, strikethrough, autolinks and alerts), parsed by markd into the
same \fB\%Document\fR model as manual pages.
.PP
Paragraphs fill, code blocks keep their lines, list items hang on their
bullet or number, block quotes get a bar per level, tables are boxed and
headings keep their level (1\-6) with a GitHub\-style anchor. Links become
\fB\%Span#link\fR targets: URLs, files relative to the document and heading
anchors. Raw HTML is dropped, keeping the text between the tags.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
doc = Docv::Markdown.parse(File.read("README.md"))
doc.anchors["installation"] # => index of the "Installation" heading block
.EE
.RE
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBALIGNS\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ALIGNS = {
  "left" => Table::CellAlign::Left,
  "center" => Table::CellAlign::Center,
  "right" => Table::CellAlign::Right,
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Table column alignments (\fB\%:\-\-\fR, \fB\%:\-:\fR, \fB\%\-\-:\fR); others are left.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBATTRIBUTES\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ATTRIBUTES = {
  Markd::Node::Type::Strong => Attr::Bold,
  Markd::Node::Type::Emphasis => Attr::Italic,
  Markd::Node::Type::Strikethrough => Attr::Strike,
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Attributes of the inline containers.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBBULLETS = ["\[u2022]", "\[u25E6]", "\[u25AA]"]\fR
List bullets by nesting depth (repeating), and the boxes of task list
items by state.
.PP
\fBCHECKBOXES = {false => "\[u2610]", true => "\[u2611]"}\fR
.PP
\fBCODE_INDENT = 4\fR
.TP 4
\fBCODE_TABS = Tabs.new(repeat: 8)\fR
Tab stops in code blocks.
.TP 4
\fBEXTENSIONS = Set {".md", ".markdown", ".mdown", ".mkd", ".mkdn"}\fR
File name extensions of Markdown documents (also with \fB\%.gz\fR).
.TP 4
\fBHTML_MARKUP = /<!\-\-.*?\-\->|<\e?.*?\e?>|<![\(ha>]*>|<\e/?[A\-Za\-z][\(ha>]*>/m\fR
Raw HTML: comments, processing instructions, declarations and tags.
.TP 4
\fBNO_BREAK = \(aq\eu00A0\(aq\fR
Code spans keep their spaces unbreakable, so they never wrap.
.TP 4
\fBOPTIONS = Markd::Options.new(gfm: true, autolink: true)\fR
Parser options: GitHub Markdown with extended autolinks (bare URLs,
\fB\%www.\fR and e\-mail addresses), and without them.
.PP
\fBPLAIN_OPTIONS = Markd::Options.new(gfm: true)\fR
.TP 4
\fBQUOTE_INDENT = 2\fR
Columns a block quote and a code block move their text right.
.TP 4
\fBSCHEME = /\eA[A\-Za\-z][A\-Za\-z0\-9+.\e\-]*:/\fR
The scheme that makes a link destination an absolute URL.
.TP 4
\fBSLUG_DROP = /[\(ha\ep{L}\ep{M}\ep{N}\ep{Pc}\e\- ]/\fR
Characters a heading anchor leaves out.
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.alert_title(node : Markd::Node) : String\fR
The title of an alert node (\fB\%> \%[!NOTE]\fR): its type as a word (\fB\%Note\fR),
or the title written after the type.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.description(text : String) : String\fR
A one\-line description of the document in \fItext\fR: its first heading
and its first paragraph, joined by a dash.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.file?(path : String) : Bool\fR
True for a file named like a Markdown document (\fB\%EXTENSIONS\fR).
.TP 4
\fBdef self.parse(text : String, highlight : Bool = false) : Document\fR
Parses Markdown \fItext\fR; with \fIhighlight\fR, code blocks labeled with a
language are syntax highlighted (\fB\%Syntax\fR).
.TP 4
\fBdef self.slug(text : String) : String\fR
The GitHub anchor of heading \fItext\fR: lower case, punctuation dropped,
spaces turned into dashes. \fB\%Document#anchors\fR adds \fB\%\-1\fR, \fB\%\-2\fR... to
repeated ones.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.tree(text : String) : Markd::Node\fR
The markd tree of \fItext\fR. Text that markd\(aqs extended autolinks cannot
handle (they can step into a multibyte character next to an \fB\%@\fR) is
parsed without them.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/markdown.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
